Adds the --num-taylor-terms option to Herbie (https://github.com/herbie-fp/herbie)
at commit 73ba1fe76f97d4cdb852a602addd82e3a983b209, the sources/herbie submodule.
It sets *taylor-order-limit*, the number of terms kept in each Taylor series
(default 2), and passes the parameter to worker places so that the option
takes effect with --threads. The GENGA drift search uses it.
Apply from the root of the Herbie tree: patch -p1 < herbie-num-taylor-terms.patch

diff --git a/src/api/server.rkt b/src/api/server.rkt
index 2a8a7344a..a24bef078 100644
--- a/src/api/server.rkt
+++ b/src/api/server.rkt
@@ -296,6 +296,7 @@
                          *reeval-pts*
                          *node-limit*
                          *max-find-range-depth*
+                         *taylor-order-limit*
                          *platform-state*)
    (activate-platform! (*platform-state*))
    ; not sure if the above code is actaully needed.
@@ -427,6 +428,7 @@
                          *reeval-pts*
                          *node-limit*
                          *max-find-range-depth*
+                         *taylor-order-limit*
                          *platform-state*)
    (activate-platform! (*platform-state*))
    (define worker-thread
diff --git a/src/main.rkt b/src/main.rkt
index 98dbde578..919f19586 100644
--- a/src/main.rkt
+++ b/src/main.rkt
@@ -103,6 +103,12 @@
      during sampling. May fix \"Cannot sample enough valid points\" but will slow."
      (format "[Default: ~a iterations]" (*max-find-range-depth*)))
     (*max-find-range-depth* (string->number num))]
+   [("--num-taylor-terms")
+    num
+    ("The maximum number of terms in each Taylor series. Herbie may find additional improvements
+     with more terms. Herbie slows down with more terms."
+     (format "[Default: ~a terms]" (*taylor-order-limit*)))
+    (*taylor-order-limit* (string->number num))]
    [("--profile") "Whether to profile each run (no-op, always on)" (void)]
    #:multi [("-o" "--disable")
             flag
diff --git a/www/doc/2.4/options.html b/www/doc/2.4/options.html
index f1beeae85..c9b3732c3 100644
--- a/www/doc/2.4/options.html
+++ b/www/doc/2.4/options.html
@@ -126,6 +126,12 @@
       algebraic reasoning. The default is 4000. Increasing this option
       will slow Herbie down, but may improve results slightly.</dd>
     
+    <dt><code>--num-taylor-terms <var>N</var></code></dt>
+    <dd>The maximum number of terms in each Taylor series that
+      Herbie uses to approximate expressions. The default is 2.
+      Increasing this option will slow Herbie down, but may find more
+      accurate series approximations.</dd>
